    "b-ks2-path-pr-intro": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-pr-intro",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "PR IMPORTED — The pr pathway ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "index_task.pathway",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pr_imported",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "). Fires when the PR importer — a small preprocessing agent — imports an external pull request. The importer archives the raw PR and its discussion into the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pr://",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " source and reconstructs the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pull_request",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " ledger row — touched files and targets, outcome, summary — through the same summary prompt the worker summary agent uses; no worker trace exists, so the row is a deduction from diff and discussion, never a fabricated trace. Pure enrichment: the librarian starts from what the PR touched, and the importer never writes facts. The librarian maps the diff to the targets and files it touched and updates their facts, citing "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pr://",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
